r and asks learners to commit to a guess about where its food comes from, so a personal wrong model is on the table. The explanation then fixes the category term \\\\u2014 the plant is a producer, a living thing that makes its own food \\\\u2014 and separates what the plant takes in through its roots from what it makes. The contrast section puts the producer idea against the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings on the same plant so the boundary is visible, and the close checks whether the learner now recognizes the plant, not the soil or the water, as the maker of the food.\"\\n    },\\n    \"neighbours\": [\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Directs learners to the select-one commitment that follows, making the elicit action visible in the document sequence without authoring the interaction itself.\",\\n        \"role\": \"practice-cue\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"heading\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Marks the shift from guessing to the fixed category term so the definition lands as the key idea of the section.\",\\n        \"role\": \"explain\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b1\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Separates what the plant takes in through its roots from what it makes, holding attention on the plant as the maker while treating soil materials and water only as intakes.\",\\n        \"role\": \"explain\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b2\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"list\",\\n        \"reason\": \"Lays out the intake-versus-made distinction as a compact pair of contrasts so the separation is easy to read at a glance without introducing sunlight as food.\",\\n        \"role\": \"explain\",\\n        \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b2\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n    \"reason\": \"States the