 idea on the same windowsill plant: the roots draw soil materials and water into the plant, but what enters through the roots is raw material the plant uses, not the plant\\'s food. The food itself is made by the plant. Hold the learner\\'s attention on the plant as the maker and treat soil and water only as intakes, so the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings are undermined without being named as errors yet. Do not introduce the sunlight-as-food idea and do not treat food and energy as interchangeable.\",\\n      \"evidence\": \"Two approved misconceptions both locate food outside the plant, so this block must relocate food-making inside it by separating \\'what the plant takes in\\' from \\'what the plant makes\\' \\\\u2014 a separation a bare definition cannot make.\",\\n      \"id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n      \"intent\": \"explain\"\\n    },\\n    \"terminology\": []\\n  },\\n  \"mode\": \"generate\",\\n  \"scoped_request\": {\\n    \"allowed_facts\": [\\n      \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n      \"living things need food to grow\",\\n      \"Plants are living things that can produce their own food\",\\n      \"Plants are called producers\",\\n      \"Use one concrete classroom example.\",\\n      \"Explain that plants make their own food (are producers)\",\\n      \"Identify leaves as the site of photosynthesis and chlorophyll as the light-capturing substance\",\\n      \"Describe photosynthesis as using light, carbon dioxide, and water to produce food and oxygen\",\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"brief\": \"Build the idea on the same windowsill plant: the roots draw soil materials and water into the plant, but what enters through the roots is raw material the plant uses, not the plant\\'s food. The food itself is made by the plant. Hold the learner\\'s attention on the plant as the maker and treat soil and water only as intakes, so the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings are undermined without be